 ## Overview
-The Cosine Decay Learning Rate Schedule reduces the learning rate over the course of training following a cosine curve, transitioning from a maximum value to a minimum value. It is designed to provide a smooth convergence path, avoiding the sharp discontinuities of step decay while ensuring the learning rate asymptotically approaches zero (or a small floor) to stabilize fine-tuning. It is distinct from the parent [Exponential Decay Schedules](18486-exponential-decay-schedules.md) by using a trigonometric function rather than an exponential one, and from [Linear Learning Rate Schedule](11850-linear-learning-rate-schedule.md) by its non-linear, curved decay profile. It is frequently paired with a linear warm-up phase to prevent early training instability [S2][S3, unofficial].
+The Cosine Decay Learning Rate Schedule reduces the learning rate over the course of training following a cosine curve, transitioning from a maximum value to a minimum value [S1, S2]. It is designed to provide a smooth convergence path, avoiding the sharp discontinuities of step decay while ensuring the learning rate asymptotically approaches zero (or a small floor) to stabilize fine-tuning [G]. It is distinct from the parent [Exponential Decay Schedules](18486-exponential-decay-schedules.md) by using a trigonometric function rather than an exponential one, and from [Linear Learning Rate Schedule](11850-linear-learning-rate-schedule.md) by its non-linear, curved decay profile [G]. It is frequently paired with a linear warm-up phase to prevent early training instability [S2][S3, unofficial].
 
